## Context

Child of 0700. First step of the redesign in `docs/rel-pipeline-redesign-2026-10-10.md`: it settles whether the scoring design works before any pool-scale scoring or paid run. It also fixes which cut and which arbiter the alpha-cut (at most 10,000 works) uses.

Inputs the author supplies: the verified Gavard set, the 50/50 test set, and a small shot set (a few positives and negatives, outside both sealed sets). The predicates are not an input: they were set by the author on 2026-10-09 and are written in `docs/rel-pipeline-redesign-2026-10-10.md` section 2.4 (research, economic, international, climate, finance, plus the computed venue and metadata gate, and the certainty fields). `config/rel_stage2_prompt_v3.md` is the earlier design and is not used unchanged. Descriptors are post-cut (section 10 of the note) and are not part of this trial except the model-knowledge check below.

Reuse of earlier paid work (reference only, never truth, never in a prompt for a sealed set): clear `out` works (6 of 51,602 stage-1 `out` works became `icf`) as extra negatives for calibration; stage-1/stage-2 disagreements and the Opus and Fable corrections as a source of hard cases for the author to pick from. Same-vendor labels (Haiku, Sol, Luna) inflate any agreement with the new experts.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The question set is frozen by the SHA-256 of its text (and of the arbiter prompt with its few-shots), and the sealed files (Gavard, 50/50 test, shot set) carry a SHA-256 recorded here before any model run, with one line per work giving the reason for the pick.
- [ ] Price derived and shown to the author before any paid call; no paid call without the author's go.
- [ ] Positive control: a known positive and a known negative behave as expected for each model and for the arbiter before any count is reported.
- [ ] Per model, a cut calibrated on the Gavard set plus a draw of clear negatives, with recall at the cut reported with a Wilson 95% interval on the 50/50 test set, by act (1990-2006, 2007-2014, 2015-2025) and by language.
- [ ] Divergent share measured; arbiter run on the divergent works with and without few-shots; a third API vendor reported as the fallback if the local arbiter fails on non-English.
- [ ] The number of works the calibrated cuts would keep on the filtered pool, stated as derived with the arithmetic shown, so the 10,000 ceiling is checked.
- [ ] A short report ending in a go, revise or stop recommendation; the author decides.
- [ ] Trial arms, each measured on the sealed sets: evidence-type `choice` questions against bare probabilities; the shared-object wording (the non-obvious negatives are the test); venue-first ordering (share of works removed before any call); Luna on the Decisions endpoint against chat-completions batch (price and agreement).
- [ ] Model-knowledge check: 20 abstracts, each model asked for OECD FORD and UN M49 codes, compared with the author's reading.
- [ ] A hard cost ceiling for the scale run, set by the author before launch (the 2026-10-10 discussion: nothing is worth USD 90; MOE suggested USD 20); nothing larger launches without the author's go.
